@startuml 08b_seq_submit
' Sequence diagram 2 — Submit an assessment or update for an existing place (v0.4, 2026-11-01)
' Changes from v0.3: the same flow runs on the public website (Next.js pages, server-side calls
' instead of /api; photos uploaded from the device); 1 to 3 photos per criterion.
!include _seq.iuml
title 2 · Submit an assessment for an existing place

actor "Registered user" as U
participant "Mobile app\nor website" as App
box "Backend · Next.js on Cloudflare" #FAFAFA
  participant "API route\n+ requireRole()" as API
  participant "Rules scoring" as Score
  database "D1" as DB
end box
participant "R2\n(photos)" as R2
participant "Email\nprovider" as Mail

note over U, App : The user is signed in and has opened an existing place.

== Choose what to report ==
U -> App : tap "Assess this place"\n(or "Update" if already rated)
App -> API : GET /api/criteria
API -> DB : criteria + questions (ro/en)
DB --> API : rows
API --> App : questionnaire
U -> App : pick criteria, answer questions

== Upload photos (1 to 3 per criterion) ==
loop for each criterion that exists at the place
  U -> App : take or choose photo\n(website: upload from the device)
  App -> API : POST /api/photos/upload-url
  API -> API : requireRole(user)
  API --> App : signed upload link\n(private "pending" area)
  App -> R2 : upload photo
  R2 --> App : stored
end
note right of App : No photo needed for\n"Not needed", "No public toilet" or "N/A".

== Submit ==
U -> App : tap "Submit"
App -> API : POST /api/submissions\nplace id, chosen criteria,\nanswers, photo keys
API -> API : requireRole(user)\nvalidate answers + photos

alt something is missing or invalid
  API --> App : 400: what to fix
  App --> U : highlight the problem\n(draft kept)
else valid
  API -> Score : answers
  Score --> API : suggested level\n+ explanation + reviewer notes
  API -> DB : one batch: PROPOSED assessment,\nanswers, photo records,\nsubmission (PENDING), suggestion,\nchange log entry
  DB --> API : ok
  API --> App : submission id, PENDING
  App --> U : "Thanks! A reviewer\nwill check it."
  API ->> Mail : after the response:\n"New submission" to reviewers
end

note over API, DB
  Nothing the user sent is public yet.
  On the website the same steps run through
  server-side calls in the same app, not /api.
  The place keeps showing its current
  (verified) information until approval.
end note
@enduml
